# Quorum — LLM configuration
#
# Everything here is OPTIONAL. With no configuration, Quorum runs entirely
# offline at zero cost and renders cluster labels from the medoid — the real
# submission closest to the cluster centre. That is a supported, permanent
# mode, not a degraded trial. See docs/adr/0005-deterministic-core-llm-at-render-edge.md
#
# There is no model identifier anywhere in the source tree. The model is a
# config value, so a deprecation or a new release is an edit to this file and
# nothing else. See docs/adr/0016-llm-is-config-not-code.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Off (the default). Medoid labels, no network, no spend.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
QUORUM_LLM_PROVIDER=none

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Free options. Pick one, uncomment it, and set a model.
#
# We deliberately do NOT print model names here — whatever we wrote would be
# wrong within months. Run this to ask the endpoint what it currently serves:
#
#   curl -s $QUORUM_LLM_BASE_URL/models \
#     -H "Authorization: Bearer $QUORUM_LLM_API_KEY" | jq -r '.data[].id'
#
# Quorum does the same automatically: if a configured model 404s, the error
# lists the models the endpoint actually offers.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Fully local — no key, no account, no limits, no data leaving the machine.
# The best answer for the "we can't send customer feedback to a third party"
# objection, and the one to reach for first.
#   QUORUM_LLM_PROVIDER=ollama
#   QUORUM_LLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
#   QUORUM_LLM_MODEL=<run: ollama list>

# Groq — free tier, OpenAI-compatible, fast.
#   QUORUM_LLM_PROVIDER=groq
#   QUORUM_LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
#   QUORUM_LLM_MODEL=<see the curl above>
#   QUORUM_LLM_API_KEY=

# Google Gemini via its OpenAI-compatible endpoint — free tier available.
#   QUORUM_LLM_PROVIDER=gemini
#   QUORUM_LLM_BASE_URL=https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai
#   QUORUM_LLM_MODEL=<see the curl above>
#   QUORUM_LLM_API_KEY=

# OpenRouter — aggregates many providers, including free-tier models.
#   QUORUM_LLM_PROVIDER=openrouter
#   QUORUM_LLM_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
#   QUORUM_LLM_MODEL=<see the curl above>
#   QUORUM_LLM_API_KEY=

# Any other OpenAI-compatible endpoint works with no code change:
# llama.cpp, vLLM, LM Studio, Together, Fireworks, DeepInfra, Anthropic and
# OpenAI compat layers, or a self-hosted gateway. Set base URL + model + key.

# Request timeout in milliseconds. Default 30000.
# QUORUM_LLM_TIMEOUT_MS=30000
